==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|NL.|paraplegia}}, from {{der|en|grc|παραπληγίη}}, Ionic Greek for {{m|grc|παραπληξία|t=paralysis on one side}}, from {{m|grc|παραπλήσσεσθαι|t=to be stricken on one side}}, active {{m|grc|παραπλήσσειν|t=to strike on one side}}, from {{m|grc|παρά|t=beside}} + {{m|grc|πλήσσειν|t=to strike}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|pathology}} A [[condition]] where the lower half of a patient's body is [[paralyzed]] and cannot move.

